        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jedreekPrograms/VintedOfferTracker/pulls/114",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/VintedOfferTracker/pull/114",
          "diff_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/VintedOfferTracker/pull/114.diff",
          "patch_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/VintedOfferTracker/pull/114.patch",
          "merged_at": null
        },
        "body": "## Problem\nVinted currently emits seller message timestamps such as `1.09.2026, 12:27:39`, while `ConversationActivityDetector` required `dd.MM.yyyy`. The detector therefore saw seller messages but persisted their activity time as null. For a PENDING conversation without a read indicator this incorrectly fell back to the 48-hour no-engagement timeout instead of the intended seller-message + 3-hour policy.\n\n## Fix\n- accept one- or two-digit day/month in Vinted timestamps via `d.M.yyyy, HH:mm:ss`\n- keep invalid/unrecognized timestamps fail-closed as null\n- add regression tests for current Vinted format, zero-padded format, single-digit day/month, and invalid input\n\nNo schema/data changes.",
        "reactions": {
